-/* -- Stage: 4A "Day Into Dusk", with the ruled composition correction --
-   Every number is measured off the approved 1440x800 and 375x700 frames. The
-   frames' chrome is 82px, exactly this site's sticky header, so their offsets
-   carry over unchanged.
-
-   ONE UNIT. --u is a length: 1px at the approved frame, shrinking with whichever
-   of width or height binds first. Every value below is calc(var(--u) * V) where
-   V is the reference pixel. The whole frame is therefore one object that scales
-   and stays centred, which is what removes the void: widths used to key to the
-   viewport while type keyed to height, so the copy and the window drifted to
-   opposite margins and the middle opened up.
-
-   RULED AMENDMENT to 4A: the window is larger (620x376 against 560x340) and sits
-   nearer centre-right (left edge 710 against 792, right margin 110 against 88),
-   so the frame reads as one composition rather than two elements at the margins. */
-.hero{padding:0;position:relative;background:var(--linen)}
-.wrap{width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 56px;box-sizing:border-box}
-
-.hh{
-  /* ΓòÉΓòÉΓòÉ THE SCALING LAW ΓòÉΓòÉΓòÉ ruled 2026-08-01. Read this before touching 485.
-
-     485 IS THE COMPOSITION'S ACTUAL NEED, NOT THE REFERENCE FRAME'S HEIGHT.
-     This distinction is the whole bug that was fixed here, and re-deriving the
-     divisor from the frame brings it straight back.
-
-     The divisor was 718, which is the approved frame's hero height (800 - 82).
-     That looks like the right number and is not, because this layout is NOT a
-     stack. Until 2026-08-01 the two columns carried two different anchors ΓÇö
-     .hh-copy pinned to the TOP at 68u, .hh-group to the BOTTOM at 72u ΓÇö so
-     what the composition needed was whichever COLUMN is taller, not the frame
-     it was drawn in. Measured at --u = 1:
-
-         copy column    396.4u + 68u offset  =  464.4u   <- binding
-         window group   367.1u + 72u offset  =  439.1u
-
-     So the composition needs 464.4u and the law was reserving 718u ΓÇö over-
-     reserving by 54.6% at every viewport. Where height binds, that shrank the
-     whole hero by a third for no reason: at 1966x594 the window rendered
-     394x239 (20% of a 1966px monitor) with 181px of the hero box sitting
-     empty, and the constellation correctly refused 7A because the band it was
-     handed was phone-sized. The figure was never the problem.
-
-         485 = 464.4 (measured need) + 4.4% margin
-
-     THE TWO PINS ARE GONE (ruled 2026-08-01, Change 1 ΓÇö see .hh-copy). Both
-     columns now centre in the band, so the +68u and +72u offsets above no
-     longer apply and the binding need is simply the taller column: 396.4u.
-
-     485 IS RETAINED DELIBERATELY. It is not a leftover. Centred, it reserves
-     (485 - 396.4) / 2 = 44.3u of breathing above and below the copy column at
-     the approved frame, and re-deriving the divisor down toward 396.4 would
-     put poster-scale type hard against the band's edges wherever height binds.
-     Do not re-derive 485 from the centred layout without Amy ruling the render;
-     tests/hero-1440x800.spec.js locks what 485 produces at the frame. If the
-     copy block changes, RE-MEASURE the taller column and re-derive from it; do
-     not scale 485 by eye and do not reach for 718 again.
-
-     THE CAP IS 1.10, NOT 1. It sets how far the composition may grow past the
-     approved frame, and it has to exceed 1 or the height term can never lift a
-     short viewport above frame size no matter what the divisor is. 1.10 lets
-     large displays render 10% larger than the 1440 frame, which is the point:
-     a 1080p monitor used to get exactly the same hero as a 1440 one.
-
-     1440x800 IS UNAFFECTED AND MUST STAY SO. There the width term is 1 and the
-     height term is 718/485 = 1.480, so the minimum is 1 exactly as before. That
-     composition is ruled, and tests/hero-1440x800.spec.js locks its geometry ΓÇö
-     if you change this line and that test fails, you moved something ruled.
-
-     Full derivation and the 20-viewport matrix: docs/hero-u-law-proposal.md */
-  --u:min(1.10px,calc(100vw / 1440),max(0.62px,calc((100vh - 82px) / 485)));
-  --u:min(1.10px,calc(100vw / 1440),max(0.62px,calc((100svh - 82px) / 485)));
-  position:relative;
-  height:calc(100vh - 82px);
-  height:calc(100svh - 82px);
-  overflow:hidden;
-  display:flex;align-items:stretch;
-  background-color:#F8F4E9;
-  background-image:radial-gradient(66% 54% at 20% 16%,rgba(255,253,245,0.80) 0%,rgba(248,244,233,0) 72%);
-}
