-          583.78px card, so 188.05px of dead column sat exactly where the
-          composition needed air taken OUT. --hh-win makes the column honest.
-          It can never widen anything ΓÇö min() picks the card where the column
-          has outgrown it and the column everywhere else, so at 1440 it
-          resolves to 552.66px, the span it already was, and the card's own
-          width, the band it hands the constellation, and SHIFT_Q are all
-          untouched at the approved frame.
-
-       2. THE GAP WAS NEVER A DECISION. It was grid column 7 plus its two
-          gutters, so it grew with the viewport: 139.34px at 1440, 183.17px at
-          1966, and it would keep going. --hh-gap replaces that arithmetic with
-          a stated interval.
-
-       THE GAP IS THE DESIGNED QUANTITY; THE FRAME IS ARITHMETIC. Do not reach
-       for a container width here and let the gap fall out of it ΓÇö that is how
-       the composition ended up keyed to the viewport in the first place. Set
-       the gap; the frame is span6 + gap + window, centred in the stage. The
